   8+ 8000              ;
   9+ 8000              ; Implemented:
  10+ 8000              ;   0000h-000Fh, 0080h-0083h: 8237 address/count, controller and page registers.
  11+ 8000              ;   0020h-0021h: 8259A master PIC register model and CPU acknowledge path.
  12+ 8000              ;   0040h-0043h: 8253 channel programming, latches and static readback.
  13+ 8000              ;   0060h-0063h: initial XT-compatible 8255 PPI / keyboard interface.
  14+ 8000              ;   00E0h: retained 16-bit diagnostic test latch.
  15+ 8000              ;   Keyboard FIFO pushes raise master-PIC IRQ1; ATM input producer remains pending.
  16+ 8000              ;   DMA transfer engine and PIT clock/IRQ0 are separate, not-yet-implemented services.
  17+ 8000              ;
  18+ 8000              ; PPI compatibility slice:
  19+ 8000              ;   60h = port A / keyboard data (FIFO consumer when configured input).
  20+ 8000              ;   61h = port B / system control; bit-6 rising edge resets XT keyboard,
  21+ 8000              ;         bit 7 acknowledges/clears the current keyboard data latch.
  22+ 8000              ;   62h = port C input/output composition.
  23+ 8000              ;   63h = mode-set and bit-set/reset control register (mode 0 implemented).
  24+ 8000              ;   PPI reset defaults follow PCem/ppi.c: PA=00h, PB=40h.
  25+ 8000              ;
  26+ 8000              ; Keyboard FIFO bytes raise PIC IRQ1 when accepted. ATM keyboard input delivery
  27+ 8000              ; remains a future DMA/IPC producer; no physical NeoGS I/O is involved.
